.TH MX-SERVICE-MANAGER 1 "2026-07-20" "MX Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mx-service-manager \- enable and disable system services
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mx-service-manager
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mx-service-manager
is a graphical tool for managing services and daemons and controlling which services are started at boot time. Read the warning in the application before changing a service: disabling a required service can leave the system partially or completely inoperable.
.PP
The application displays the available services and their current state. Use it to enable or disable services manually and to inspect service descriptions before making changes.
.SH OPTIONS
This application has no documented command-line options. The graphical interface provides all operations.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/mx-service-manager
Installed HTML help, images, license, and changelog documentation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR service (8)
.SH AUTHOR
MX Linux contributors.
